    "laws": [
      "array length is fixed and an out-of-range get returns none",
      "array set and strong compare-exchange linearize one slot without spurious success",
      "map replacement preserves position and remove/reinsert appends a fresh generation",
      "set duplicate insertion is a false no-op and remove is idempotent",
      "stack is LIFO and queue is FIFO without destructive peek or snapshot",
      "map compare-exchange distinguishes absent, mismatch, replacement and removal",
      "every bounded operation is checked against an independent sequential state",
      "histories preserve real-time precedence while searching all permitted linearizations",
      "direct cursors capture a finite structural horizon without copying contents",
      "cursor generations are yielded at most once under removal, replacement and reinsertion",
      "stack and queue cursors never consume their source",
      "aliases share identity and the last handle or cursor performs cleanup exactly once",
      "stale handles and cursors fail closed before state access",
      "bounded fuzz schedules are deterministic, panic-free and leak-free"
    ],
    "sequence_seeds": 4096,
    "oracle": "independent bounded sequential state, exhaustive history search and cursor invariants",
